# Copy to bot/.env (git-ignored). Variables already set in the shell win over this file.
# The repo-root .env is also read, after bot/.env.

# Signing keys. MIRROR_/KEEPER_ override DEPLOYER_ for that bot. Never printed.
DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=
# MIRROR_PRIVATE_KEY=
# KEEPER_PRIVATE_KEY=
# The sealed-oracle bot signs with SEALED_KEY, else KEEPER_PRIVATE_KEY. Give it its own key: it sends a poke every
# block or two, which would race the keeper for nonces.
# SEALED_KEY=

# Chain
# DEPLOYMENTS_FILE=../deployments/unichain-sepolia.json
# One URL, or several comma-separated: the first is primary, the rest are fallbacks in order
# RPC_URL=https://sepolia.unichain.org
# CHAIN_ID=1301
# DRY_RUN=0
# ONCE=0
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# TX_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# Address overrides (otherwise read from DEPLOYMENTS_FILE)
# POOL_MANAGER=
# PREDICTION_HOOK=
# The ownerless MarketGatekeeper that owns PREDICTION_HOOK, and its MarketSchedulers (one per track, comma-separated,
# in the gatekeeper's order). The keeper calls every scheduler's open(), which anyone may call
# MARKET_GATEKEEPER=
# MARKET_SCHEDULERS=
# UNDERLYING_ORACLE=
# PRICE_STEERER=
# DEMO_WETH=
# DEMO_USDC=
# Only to pin the underlying pool: the mirror reads the key from the oracle's poolKey() and refuses a pinned mismatch
# UNDERLYING_POOL_FEE=500
# UNDERLYING_POOL_TICK_SPACING=10

# Price mirror
# MIRROR_INTERVAL_MS=1000
# MIRROR_THRESHOLD_BPS=2
# coinbase, kraken, binanceus quote <SYM>-USD; binance quotes <SYM>USDT
# MIRROR_SOURCES=coinbase,kraken,binanceus
# MIRROR_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS=2500
# MIRROR_MAX_JUMP_BPS=1000
# The mirror steers every entry of `underlyings` in DEPLOYMENTS_FILE (or, without it, the single demoWeth pool as ETH).
# MIRROR_SYMBOLS keeps only the listed ones, e.g. ETH or ETH,SOL (default: all)
# MIRROR_SYMBOLS=
# Feed prices outside a per-asset band are dropped. Defaults: ETH 100..100000, SOL 5..2000, BTC 1000..10000000; any
# other symbol needs both of its own. MIRROR_MIN_PRICE / MIRROR_MAX_PRICE are the older ETH-only names.
# MIRROR_ETH_MIN_PRICE=100
# MIRROR_ETH_MAX_PRICE=100000
# MIRROR_SOL_MIN_PRICE=5
# MIRROR_SOL_MAX_PRICE=2000

# Keeper schedule. One keeper drives every track: it calls each scheduler's permissionless open(), which opens one
# market per slot of block.timestamp / period, with the period read from that scheduler's config() (a failed read stops
# the keeper at start-up). Right after a slot boundary the latest block can still be in the previous slot, so
# AlreadyOpened for that older slot is retried every poll until a block of the new slot lands. AlreadyOpened for the new
# slot means another caller opened it first. A TooLate slot, or one with less than KEEPER_MIN_TRADE_SEC of trading left,
# is skipped.
# KEEPER_POLL_MS=2000
# KEEPER_MIN_TRADE_SEC=5
# KEEPER_ALIGN=1
# KEEPER_CREATE=1
# KEEPER_SETTLE=1
# KEEPER_SCAN_BACK=50
# Seconds past expiry before settleInvalid; raised to the hook's GRACE + 1 (3601) if lower
# KEEPER_INVALID_AFTER_SEC=3601

# Sealed-oracle poker and prover (npm run sealed). SEALED_ORACLE overrides `sealedOracle` in DEPLOYMENTS_FILE.
# SEALED_ORACLE=
# Most proofs per proveMany (1-64, ~0.72M gas each). A batch is halved while its gas estimate fails or exceeds half a
# block or 5/6 of EIP-7825's 16,777,216 per-transaction cap.
# SEALED_BATCH=16
# SEALED_POLL_MS=500
# Read-only RPCs tried after RPC_URL for headers and eth_getProof, comma-separated. Recovering from an outage needs one
# that serves eth_getProof for old blocks, an archive node (docs/md/RUNBOOK.md section 8). The bot warns at start-up
# when no RPC serves a proof 300 blocks back.
# SEALED_RPC_FALLBACKS=

# Market timing, quote and budget are not bot settings: the MarketScheduler fixes them at deploy time from the repo-root
# .env (SCHEDULER_*, MARKET_*, QUOTE_*, see docs/md/RUNBOOK.md section 3).
